{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJhxL3kveCFBCUKki4w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KPdkRzqA15atHJE1hnMvUM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-hiMTYs/memory/log-lines-no-customer-pii.md","content":"---\nname: log-lines-no-customer-pii\ndescription: Privacy rule from security review: log lines must never contain a customer's name or email; refer to customers by id only (e.g. cus_002)\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA log line must never contain a customer's name or email address. When a log line needs to refer to a customer, use their id (e.g. `cus_002`) and nothing else.\n\n**Why:** Log lines are sent to a third-party log service, and the security review ruled that customer PII must not go there.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code that writes logs (logger calls, print/debug output, error messages that get logged, exception text), log only the customer id. Don't interpolate customer name, email, or whole customer objects/dicts that contain them. Check this when adding or reviewing logging code.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9675,"cache_read_input_tokens":11962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9675,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5f69288-5387-481f-bd5b-bf631ad22355","uuid":"09902817-296f-4214-a939-7f93344feb43","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:30:51.234Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJhwxUD8DncrzWzQwkx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KPdkRzqA15atHJE1hnMvUM":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-hiMTYs/memory/log-lines-no-customer-pii.md","content":"---\nname: log-lines-no-customer-pii\ndescription: Privacy rule from security review: log lines must never contain a customer's name or email; refer to customers by id only (e.g. cus_002)\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA log line must never contain a customer's name or email address. When a log line needs to refer to a customer, use their id (e.g. `cus_002`) and nothing else.\n\n**Why:** Log lines are sent to a third-party log service, and the security review ruled that customer PII must not go there.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code that writes logs (logger calls, print/debug output, error messages that get logged, exception text), log only the customer id. Don't interpolate customer name, email, or whole customer objects/dicts that contain them. Check this when adding or reviewing logging code.\n"}}}
